  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1073,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 1089,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151463,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 39,
        "headingId": 1089,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> Skene&rsquo;s gland adenocarcinoma, periurethral gland adenocarcinoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:18:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1074,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 1090,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151464,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 39,
        "headingId": 1090,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:18:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1075,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 1091,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151465,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 39,
        "headingId": 1091,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Skene glands occur in the anterior vagina and distal one&nbsp;third of the female urethra; thus, these tumours, which arise from these minor vestibular glands, are typically localized to periurethral/paraurethral, urethral, anterior vaginal wall, and bladder neck locations {14668555; 9584326; 7525428; 3114949; 28872768; 7507278; 20870432; 29901570; 29439715; 31883942; 32504685; 32795117; 34706525; 35192863}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:18:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1076,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 1092,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151466,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 39,
        "headingId": 1092,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The usual presentation is with a mass and (less frequently) haematuria or incontinence. Serum PSA may be elevated {14668555; 20870432; 7525428; 29901570; 29439715; 32504685}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:18:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1077,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 1093,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151467,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 39,
        "headingId": 1093,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>This extremely rare tumour has been reported in patients ranging in age from&nbsp;46 to 88&nbsp;years (median: 71&nbsp;years) {14668555; 9584326; 7525428; 3114949; 28872768; 7507278; 20870432; 29901570; 29439715; 31883942; 32504685; 32795117; 34706525; 35192863}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:18:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1078,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 1094,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151468,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 39,
        "headingId": 1094,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:18:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1079,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 1095,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151469,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 39,
        "headingId": 1095,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours arise from the periurethral Skene glands, the female equivalent of the prostate gland in male individuals. A frameshift variant in the <em>PTEN</em> gene with loss of heterozygosity was demonstrated in one case {32795117}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:18:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1086,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 1102,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151470,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 39,
        "headingId": 1102,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours may present as a polypoid nodule or flat tumour, 0.3&ndash;3.5&nbsp;cm in size {29901570; 31883942; 34706525; 35192863}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:18:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1080,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 1096,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151471,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 39,
        "headingId": 1096,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These neoplasms are usually morphologically similar to prostatic acinar adenocarcinoma. Typically, there is a population of well-formed to poorly formed glands lined by cuboidal or columnar epithelium, with pale or eosinophilic cytoplasm, round nuclei, and prominent nucleoli. A cribriform pattern is common, and individual glands, solid areas, or a single-file pattern can be seen. The degree of nuclear atypia is variable. Goblet cells are rarely seen. Residual non-neoplastic Skene glands or foci resembling high-grade prostatic intraepithelial neoplasia may be present. Immunohistochemically, Skene gland adenocarcinoma is generally positive for prostatic markers such as PSA, PAP, NKX3-1, and P501S {14668555; 9584326; 7525428; 3114949; 28872768; 7507278; 20870432; 29901570}. AMACR expression has been present in some of the reported cases {29901570; 31883942; 32795117}. CK7 is generally negative {20870432; 28872768; 31883942; 32504685; 32795117; 34706525}. CK20 is positive in some cases {28872768; 29901570; 31883942}. AR may be positive.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:18:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1081,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 1097,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151472,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 39,
        "headingId": 1097,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:18:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1082,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 1098,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151473,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 39,
        "headingId": 1098,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:18:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1085,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 1101,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151474,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 39,
        "headingId": 1101,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> adenocarcinoma morphologically resembling prostatic adenocarcinoma; positivity for prostatic markers.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:18:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1083,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 1099,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151475,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 39,
        "headingId": 1099,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These neoplasms are staged using the FIGO and TNM staging systems.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:18:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1084,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 1100,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 151476,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 39,
        "headingId": 1100,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Experience with this neoplasm is limited. Although several cases with inguinal or pelvic lymph node metastases have been documented {9584326; 32504685; 35192863}, no recurrence or disease-related mortality was observed in the few cases with clinical follow-up after treatment {35192863}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T18:18:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]